flat_hashes_0.35.0.txt: SHA-256 digests of the outputs of the 0.35.0 release commit
(35c1558d0ce8d498230d27d96d1817e195aef321), before any skyline code existed.

One line per shipped scenario under scenarios/ whose text names one of the kinds the skyline
is wired into (orbit, integrity, gnss-sim, jamming, leo-pvt, leo-pass), including campaigns
that compose them:  <file> <sha256(json)> <sha256(svg)> <sha256(summary)>  as returned by
kshana::api::run_toml. One line per training scenario under scenarios/training/:
training/<file> <sha256(nmea_text)> from kshana::nmea_synth::gen::generate.

Generated by running, in a worktree of that commit, an integration test that iterates the
files in name order and writes the digests (the same loop tests/skyline_scenarios.rs runs).
These are the engine's own earlier outputs: they show backward compatibility, they are not an
external oracle.
